cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "Monograph PDF"
message: "Cite Monograph PDF and record the platform plus release tag or commit used. This repository citation does not assert a published release."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Mun"
    given-names: "Aung Ye"
    email: "aungyemun25@gmail.com"
license: "AGPL-3.0-or-later"
repository-code: "https://github.com/aungyemun/monograph-pdf"
abstract: >
  An offline desktop application for viewing, editing, organizing, converting,
  protecting and signing PDF documents. Supports form filling and design, text
  and image editing, merge/split/rotate, layout-preserving PDF to Word
  conversion, Office and image to PDF, AES-256 password protection with
  permissions, watermarks, visual signatures, true redaction and offline OCR
  (English and Japanese, with more languages installable). Monograph PDF connects
  to the network for optional update checks and explicit OCR-language downloads;
  automatic checks are off by default. Optional Office conversion uses a locally installed suite.
keywords:
  - PDF
  - PDF editor
  - PDF forms
  - PDF to Word
  - document conversion
  - OCR
  - Windows
  - Linux
  - macOS
  - offline
